    <string name="ui_9564adb6" formatted="false">Select a port on the Devices page. Defaults are 115200 / 8N1 / no flow control. The target rate is not measured. Check Parameters first.</string>
    <string name="ui_1d3db38" formatted="false">OK</string>
    <string name="ui_a2b7b" formatted="false">About</string>
    <string name="ui_e9f8d086" formatted="false">Serial Assistant 1.0</string>
    <string name="ui_5a1f6a83" formatted="false">Thanks: usb-serial-for-android, AndroidX and Kotlin.</string>
    <string name="ui_b3f37f9a" formatted="false">WCH Android SDK package 2.3 is included. Select WchOfficial to query the chip, clock, UART errors and GPIO. Capabilities depend on the device. This SDK exposes no reset API.</string>
    <string name="ui_100727" formatted="false">Contact</string>
    <string name="ui_134af1c9" formatted="false">Connection and rate</string>
    <string name="ui_dd8dfa91" formatted="false">Primary targets are Xiaomi 15 Pro and CH340G. Device acceptance is pending. VID/PID alone does not prove the CH340G variant.</string>
    <string name="ui_a42189a9" formatted="false">Measure UART bit width with an independent instrument. The target is 1152000 ±1%. Requested, reported, estimated and measured rates remain separate. 1200000 does not pass.</string>
    <string name="ui_b68b733b" formatted="false">Start bits are fixed at 1. Driver capabilities control other parameters. Disabled actions show the capability state. Read errors are reported separately.</string>
    <string name="ui_3b8074c0" formatted="false">Data, files and terminal</string>
    <string name="ui_680547d7" formatted="false">Transmit counts show bytes accepted by USB. They do not prove delivery to the peer. A partial write never repeats the whole command.</string>
    <string name="ui_b459b0ce" formatted="false">Queue overflow and display trimming have separate counters. A raw serial stream cannot quantify communication loss. Peer sequence numbers and checks are required.</string>
    <string name="ui_648340c5" formatted="false">Xmodem supports checksum, CRC and 1K sending. Each wait lasts 10 s. A send permits up to 3 retries. File reception is outside scope.</string>
    <string name="ui_307c98b" formatted="false">VT100 starts at 80×24. It supports cursor movement, erase, scroll regions, text attributes, cursor save and restore, and common keys. Change dimensions in Settings.</string>
    <string name="ui_e4714d06" formatted="false">The 11 AT commands address the peer modem. ATE1 enables modem echo. Use Stop to cancel the sequence.</string>
    <string name="ui_2d7c37fe" formatted="false">Lock screen and background</string>
    <string name="ui_d0be306d" formatted="false">A connectedDevice foreground service owns connections. The notification opens the app or disconnects all ports. Use system notification and battery settings.</string>
    <string name="ui_ee5c64b8" formatted="false">Lock-screen operation needs Xiaomi 15 Pro testing. After process restart, the app checks devices and permission again. It never restores a false connected state.</string>
    <string name="ui_fe4470e9" formatted="false">Internal log files</string>
